BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 72 720 Td (The Marlow Lighthouse: A Short History) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Marlow Lighthouse was completed in 1874 on the granite headland) Tj T* (north of Marlow harbour. Its tower stands 41 metres tall and was built) Tj T* (from locally quarried stone by the engineer Edwin Thorncastle.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The original lamp burned colza oil and was visible for eleven nautical) Tj T* (miles on a clear night. A clockwork rotation gave the light its) Tj T* (distinctive pattern of two flashes every twelve seconds.) Tj ET
